# DeepSeek-V4.1-Flash RT real-text A/B: cold-route share from original-el8's on-device route counter (MEGA_COUNT),
# cumulative int64 [40 layers x 384 experts] dumped by the hook; snapshots taken around each concurrency block
# (start -> after-c1 -> after-c16 -> after-c32) after a forced eager pass with a unique ~410-token real-text
# CNN snippet. Block counts = difference of two snapshots, so they include that block's warm-up invocations
# and one snippet. cold = experts in rowmap-mix-v1's per-layer 'cold' list (99 of 384 per layer, published by
# original-el8); uniform routing would put 99/384 = 25.8% of routes on them. Prefill and decode tokens are both
# counted (long is prefill-heavy: 8K in per 1,024 out; short is decode-heavy). Every per-layer line is listed.
# Excerpt: lines selected verbatim from the raw files named below; hostnames, IPs, user names and GPU UUIDs
# replaced with <placeholders>. Nothing else edited. Times are Pacific (PT) unless the line says otherwise.

